# Check the file list before upload

Before `git add`, commit, push, or a Netlify deploy, inspect every path that would leave the machine. Read `git status` and the staged diff. Do not rely on memory of what was edited.

Leave these out:

- `.env` and any file with keys, tokens, or passwords. `.env.example` with placeholders is allowed.
- `node_modules/`, `.next/`, `out/`, `dist/`, `*.tsbuildinfo`, logs
- `AGENTS.md`, `CLAUDE.md`
- One-off routes and scratch such as `app/dev-link-check/`, `app/dev-*/`, `/tmp/`, `/scratch/`
- Fixtures, screenshots, and dumps created only to verify a change locally
- `.vercel/` and `.netlify/`

If such a file is present, delete it or leave it unstaged. Do not rename it to sneak it into the commit. Tell the user which paths were held back.

`pnpm-lock.yaml`, source, and `.cursor/rules/` stay in the repository.
